            <ArticleTitle>Total Synthesis of Repeating Unit of O-Polysaccharide of Providencia alcalifaciens O22 via One-Pot Glycosylation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5466-5469</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02791</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first total synthesis of the phosphorylated trisaccharide repeating unit of Providencia alcalifaciens O22 is reported. The trisaccharide contains rare deoxyamino sugar AAT at the reducing end and d-glyceramide 2-phosphate at the other end. The efficient synthesis involves one-pot assembly of trisaccharide and late-stage phosphorylation as key steps.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
